\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Accuracy--Interpretability trade-off across datasets with gTransformer. The table shows AUC scores for the predictions of the ablated configuration ($p_{\text  {sup}1}$), predictions of the grounded configuration ($p_{\text  {sup}2}$), interpretable predictions ($p_{\text  {ref}}$), and classical BKT predictions ($p_{\text  {bkt}}$). \textit  {Int. Drop} measures the representational cost of grounding ($p_{\text  {sup}1} - p_{\text  {sup}2}$), \textit  {Int. Cost} measures total interpretability cost ($p_{\text  {sup}1} - p_{\text  {ref}}$), while \textit  {Int. Gain} measures ($p_{\text  {ref}} - p_{\text  {bkt}}$).\relax }}{21}{table.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
